CRYSTAL UNIT-CELL
============================================================
This file is a compact, human-readable template and quick-
reference for crystallographic unit-cell (crystal system) 
conventions. It defines notation, diagrams, and the key 
properties of the seven crystal systems, plus a compact 
operator table.
============================================================

GENERIC TEMPLATE
Axes:
  x = e1
  y = e2
  z = e3

Length markers:
  (=)   equal length
  (≠)   distinct length

Angle markers:
  +     right angle (90°)
  / \   oblique angle (≠ 90°)
  XXX°  explicit numeric angle (e.g. 120°)

RDG Triad:
  S = Structure   (length relations)
  I = Interaction (angle relations)
  D = Dynamics    (symmetry operators)

SYSTEM_NAME
S: |e1| RELATION |e2| RELATION |e3|
I: ∠(e1,e2) = ANGLE1 ,  ∠(e2,e3) = ANGLE2 ,  ∠(e1,e3) = ANGLE3
D: {LIST_OF_SYMMETRY_OPERATORS}

  - Conventional axis choice (e.g. unique axis b = y)
  - Special constraints (e.g. α = β = γ ≠ 90°)
  - Centering type if extending to Bravais lattices

Skeleton:

        z (Lz)
        |
        |
        +------ y (Ly)
       /
      x (Lx)

Flexible angle placement examples:
  • Orthogonal: use “+”
  • Oblique: use “/” or “\” with angle label
  • Explicit: write the degree value next to the edge

Sections 0–7: one block per crystal system:
------------------------------------------------------------
Cubic 
— e1=e2=e3, all angles 90°, symmetry C4x/C4y/C4z, sketch.

Tetragonal
— e1=e2≠e3, all 90°, symmetry C4z.

Orthorhombic 
— e1≠e2≠e3, all 90°, symmetries C2x/C2y/C2z.

Hexagonal 
— e1=e2≠e3, angles: (e1,e2)=120°, others 90°, symmetry C6z.

Trigonal (Rhombohedral) 
— e1=e2=e3, α=β=γ≠90°, symmetry C3.

Monoclinic 
— e1≠e2≠e3, single oblique angle β = ∠(x,z), unique axis b = y, symmetry C2y or σ.

Triclinic 
— all lengths and angles distinct, no symmetry.

------------------------------------------------------------
0. LEGEND
------------------------------------------------------------
Axes:
  x = e1
  y = e2   (conventional monoclinic unique axis)
  z = e3

Length markers:
  (=)   equal length
  (≠)   distinct length

Angle markers:
  +     right angle (90°)
  / \   oblique angle (≠ 90°)
 120°   explicit hexagonal basal angle

RDG Triad:
  S = Structure (length relations)
  I = Interaction (angle relations)
  D = Dynamics (symmetry operators)

------------------------------------------------------------
1. CUBIC
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| = |e3|
I: all angles = 90°
D: C4x, C4y, C4z

        z
        |
        |
        +------ y
       /
      x

------------------------------------------------------------
2. TETRAGONAL
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: all angles = 90°
D: C4z

        z (≠)
        |
        |
        +------ y (=)
       /
      x (=)

------------------------------------------------------------
3. ORTHORHOMBIC
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| ≠ |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: all angles = 90°
D: C2x, C2y, C2z

        z (≠)
        |
        |
        +------ y (≠)
       /
      x (≠)

------------------------------------------------------------
4. HEXAGONAL
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: ∠(e1,e2)=120°, ∠(e1,e3)=90°, ∠(e2,e3)=90°
D: C6z

  - Hexagonal basal plane angle (x,y) = 120° is correctly shown.

        z (≠)
        |
        |
       / 120°
      x (=)
       \
        y (=)

------------------------------------------------------------
5. TRIGONAL (RHOMBOHEDRAL)
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| = |e2| = |e3|
I: α = β = γ ≠ 90°
D: C3

  - All three edges equal.
  - All three angles equal and oblique (α=β=γ≠90°).

        z (=)
       /
      /  α
     x (=)
      \
       y (=)

------------------------------------------------------------
6. MONOCLINIC (UNIQUE AXIS b = y)
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| ≠ |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: ∠(x,y)=90°, ∠(y,z)=90°, ∠(x,z)=β≠90°
D: C2y or σ

  - Conventional unique axis is b = y.
  - Single oblique angle is β = ∠(x,z).

        z (≠)
        \
         \  β
          x (≠)

        +------ y (≠)

------------------------------------------------------------
7. TRICLINIC
------------------------------------------------------------
S: |e1| ≠ |e2| ≠ |e3|
I: α ≠ β ≠ γ, all ≠ 90°
D: none

  - All lengths distinct.
  - All angles distinct and non-orthogonal.

        z (≠)
        \
         \  γ
          x (≠)
           \
            \  α
             y (≠)

